## Tests for all TeamController endpoints
## adminToken=admin | managerToken=Lynx (manager TEAM_ALPHA) | memberWithATeamToken=Rogue (member TEAM_ALPHA)
## memberWithoutATeamToken=user without team (becomes manager of Team Test) | memberWithoutATeam2=another user without team
## lastMemberInTeamToken=Pulse (member TEAM_ALPHA)

## GET /teams
### [OK 200] List all teams — member with a team (emails null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams
Accept: application/json
Authorization: {{memberWithATeamToken}}

### [OK 200] List all teams — unauthenticated visitor (emails null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams
Accept: application/json

## GET /teams/{teamId}
### [OK 200] Get TEAM_ALPHA — unauthenticated visitor (email null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/1
Accept: application/json

### [OK 200] Get TEAM_ALPHA — simple member (email null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: {{memberWithATeamToken}}

### [OK 200] Get TEAM_ALPHA — manager (email visible)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

### [OK 200] Get TEAM_ALPHA — admin (email visible)
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

### [KO 404] Get team with non-existent id
GET {{baseUrl}}/teams/999999
Accept: application/json

## POST /teams
### [KO 403] Create team — unauthenticated visitor
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Team"
}

### [OK 201] Create team — member without team (becomes manager of Team Test)
## After this test: memberWithoutATeamToken is manager of Team Test
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{memberWithoutATeamToken}}

{
  "name": "Team Test"
}

### [KO 403] Create team — member already in a team
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{memberWithATeamToken}}

{
  "name": "Team Impossible"
}

### [KO 403] Create team — manager already in a team
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

{
  "name": "Second Team"
}

### [KO 403] Create team — name already exists (case-insensitive)
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{memberWithoutATeam2}}

{
  "name": "team_alpha"
}

### [KO 400] Create team — empty name (@NotBlank)
POST {{baseUrl}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: {{memberWithoutATeam2}}

{
  "name": ""
}

### [KO 400] Designate — manager designates themselves (id=1)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/second-manager/1
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

### [KO 400] Designate — non-manager tries to designate
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/second-manager/2
Authorization: {{memberWithATeamToken}}

### [KO 400] Designate — non-existent member
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/second-manager/999999
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

### [OK 200] Designate — Lynx designates Rogue (id=2) as co-manager
## After this test: Rogue is co-manager of TEAM_ALPHA
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/second-manager/2
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

### [KO 400] Designate — co-manager already exists
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/second-manager/8
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

## PATCH /teams/{teamId}/manager/renounce
## Prérequis: Rogue (id=2) est co-manager de TEAM_ALPHA suite au test Designate ci-dessus
### [KO 400] Renounce — utilisateur non-manager de l'équipe essaie de céder le rôle
## memberWithoutATeamToken n'est pas manager de TEAM_ALPHA (il est manager de Team Test)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/manager/renounce
Authorization: {{memberWithoutATeamToken}}

### [OK 200] Renounce — Lynx (manager principal) cède le rôle à Rogue (co-manager)
## Après ce test: Rogue est manager principal, il n'y a plus de co-manager
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/manager/renounce
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

## PATCH /teams/{teamId}/leave
### [OK 204] Leave — simple member (Pulse leaves TEAM_ALPHA)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/leave
Authorization: {{lastMemberInTeamToken}}

### [OK 204] Leave — manager with co-manager (Lynx leaves, Rogue becomes manager)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/leave
Authorization: {{managerToken}}

### [KO 400] Leave — user not in the team
## memberWithoutATeamToken is in Team Test (id=3), not in TEAM_ALPHA (id=1)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/1/leave
Authorization: {{memberWithoutATeamToken}}

### [OK 204] Leave — manager alone in their team should be able to leave
## Expected behavior: 204 (team becomes inactive)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/3/leave
Authorization: {{memberWithoutATeamToken}}

### [KO 400] Leave — non-existent team
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/teams/999999/leave
Authorization: {{adminToken}}


